    [Doc][Misc] Update MiniMax-M3 deployment and tuning guide (#18575)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Synchronize the entire main-branch MiniMax-M3 guide with #18581 at
    `33c894a14`. The complete Markdown file matches that source PR except
    for the Introduction's branch label: this main-targeted guide references
    the main branch. Rebase this branch onto upstream main `fc600000`; the
    upstream MiniMax-M3 document had no intervening changes, and the rebase
    completed without conflicts.
    
    - Section 3.1 uses a four-column table for BF16, W8A8, MXFP8 and
    EAGLE3-GQA weights, with hardware requirements, ModelScope download
    links, dynamic C8/FP8 KV-cache notes and draft-model identification.
    - Chapter 5 is organized as single-node (5.1), multi-node (5.2), sub-1M
    context PD (5.3.1) and pooled PD (5.3.2), 1M context (5.4), and
    multimodal/ViT DP (5.5). Update subsection numbers, topology table
    references and internal links. Use a plain Chapter 5 heading, consistent
    tab labels and selectable platform/weight-format panels. The 950DT 1M
    panel contains nested TP8/PP1 and TP4/PP2 layout tabs.
    - All regular context-limit settings use 133000. Keep A3 1M at 1049600
    and both 950DT 1M layouts at 1048576. Retain the historical accuracy
    scores and explain that the unified configuration entries do not
    represent a fresh accuracy evaluation.
    - Keep eager execution in all four P templates. D and mixed-serving
    examples use FULL_DECODE_ONLY on A3 and 950DT, including the 1M and
    parser snippets. Preserve the omitted-by-default capture-size setting
    and update its explanatory example.
    - All 14 complete speculative configurations use consistent
    single-quoted JSON with a shell splice that expands EAGLE3_WEIGHT_PATH
    correctly. Preserve every existing JSON field, including draft KV dtype.
    Explain the A3 long-prefill threshold and allow FLASHCOMM1 with
    language-model-only for text-only serving.
    - The Introduction references the vLLM-Ascend main branch; all A3
    product references use Atlas 800I A3.
    
    Preserve the earlier deployment and tuning changes: named-variable
    launchers, per-node topology tables, A3 three-node 1P1D with P
    DP1/TP4/PP4 and global D DP8/TP4/PP1 across two machines, 950DT two-node
    PD and optional three-node Decode scaling, ordered environment exports,
    MRV2 in all 20 serving snippets, and the HCCL-buffer/short-input tuning
    table. The pooled examples retain MultiConnector, per-worker Mooncake
    segments of 15GB on A3 and 64GB on 950DT, SSD offload and local
    path/mount guidance, Master offload enablement, aligned SSD I/O buffers,
    and fragmentation/headroom sizing guidance. Preserve the A3 Prefill
    recommendations from #18427/#18453 and the original #18579 /
    yingyingzizi/vllm-ascend#1 contributions and credits.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only; no runtime code changes. Users fill named
    IP/NIC/weight paths and use the matching launcher and role template.
    Three-node 1P1D means one P service group and one D service group, with
    D spanning two machines. This synchronization does not claim new
    performance or accuracy results.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Verified that the document matches #18581 at `33c894a14` except for
    the Introduction's main-branch wording. The PR diff against the updated
    main contains only `docs/source/tutorials/models/MiniMax-M3.md`.
    - Freshly syntax-checked 43 deployment/parser Bash blocks, parsed the
    Python launcher and three JSON configurations, rendered the document
    with the MkDocs tab/superfence extensions, and verified all internal
    anchor links.
    - Checked MRV2 in all 20 serving snippets, eager execution in the four P
    commands, FULL_DECODE_ONLY in all 16 remaining snippets, 133000 regular
    limits, unchanged 1M limits and Atlas 800I naming.
    - Source PR validation already covers 18 stub-expanded complete serving
    commands, all 14 expanded draft-weight paths, environment ordering and
    local browser clicks through the BF16/W8A8 and 1M platform/layout tabs.
    All serving examples remain identical to that source PR.
    - codespell, typos, markdownlint and git diff --check passed. The full
    format.sh ci attempt was blocked during dependency installation; a
    full-suite pass is not claimed.
    - No live service change, fresh NPU benchmark, new accuracy evaluation
    or SSD hardware validation was performed for this documentation
    synchronization.
    
